<http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00006950> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                  owl:versionIRI <http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00006950> ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/conforms_to_gpad> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/modelstate> "development" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7646-0052"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date> "2026-10-27"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "Positive regulation of gluconeogenesis by OXM/GCGR (Human)"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/pav/providedBy> "http://geneontology.org"^^xsd:string ,
                                                                                   "https://www.uniprot.org" ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "2026-10-13: GCGR, GNAS, ADCY6, PKA moved from part_of GO:0007189 to part_of GO:0045722 'positive regulation of gluconeogenesis', same evidence as the glucagon model gomodel:6ab067da00007273 (see its comment: GCGR IDA PMID:35767325 + ISS MGI:99572; GNAS ISS MGI:95777 PMID:16239968; ADCY6 ISS MGI:87917 PMID:31918924, indirect; PKA ISS MGI:97592 PMID:23292513). OXM hormone activity deliberately LEFT on GO:0007189: PubMed search found no data showing native OXM drives gluconeogenesis (only rat hepatocyte glycine cleavage PMID:9365819, mouse glycogenolysis PMID:22421924, and synthetic OXM-based/dual-agonist pharmacology)."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Built by claude4go with curator 2026-10-12; source table reviewed and corrected (MF specificity, cAMP small-molecule link, one CREB1 unit per target, evidence). Mostly abstract-level evidence; full texts not read."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "GNAS->ADCY6: human ADCY6 activated by Galpha-s in vitro (PMID:17110384, abstract; Gs species not stated) -> IC. ADCY6 choice for hepatocyte: mouse glucagon/ADCY6/cAMP/PKA/CREB pathway in hepatocytes (PMID:31918924)."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "OXM->GCGR: rat hepatocytes, OXM (1 uM) stimulates glycine cleavage flux, ~40% blocked by GCGR antagonist (PMID:9365819, abstract) -> ISS from rat Gcg/Gcgr. OXM is a low-affinity GCGR agonist; its main receptor is GLP1R. Supporting: hamster insulinoma OXM displaces glucagon binding (PMID:8828464); mouse OXM GCGR agonism/liver glycogenolysis (PMID:22421924)."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "PKA->CREB1 Ser133: PMID:2573431 (rat PC12) -> ISS RGD. CRTC2: mouse TORC2 regulates fasting gluconeogenic CREB transcription (PMID:16148943) -> ISS MGI. CREB1->PCK1/G6PC1: mouse CREB mutants reduce gluconeogenic gene expression (PMID:11557984) -> ISS MGI; note that in that study CREB acts largely via PGC-1 (not modelled). Not modelled: PKA-SIK2 control of CRTC2, CBP/p300, PGC-1alpha."^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <https://w3id.org/biolink/vocab/in_taxon> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606> .

